{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PROVEN RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1, 2026-08-09)\n\nRoot cause: `material_basis()` canonicalizes the description but inserts operator free text `no_file_impact_reason` byte-for-byte whenever `file_impact_scope == \"none\"` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py:119-135`). `material_fingerprint()` then JSON-serializes and hashes that basis (`pass1.py:739-770`). The raw insertion is the first divergence; serialization only faithfully preserves it.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof used a fixed `PlanContext` with scope=`none`, identical description/file impact/children, and changed only the reason. Baseline `docs only` => `1f987a8683504420`; trailing space => `bc423348886c26f3`; trailing newline => `54adef751fa61586`; leading blank line => `48965da49efade62`. At the exact gate seam, `plan_review_status()` reported `certified` for baseline and `stale-material` for each whitespace-only variant. `material_basis()` showed the only differing value was the raw nested reason. Normalizing only the reason in the experimental input with the existing `normalize_insignificant_whitespace()` restored the baseline fingerprint exactly. This confirms the raw-reason artifact and rejects a serializer defect.\n\nRivals rejected: (1) field-scope logic is not causal because scope remained `none` in every main trial; the separate scope control correctly removed the entire component for `paths`, which is a meaningful state change. (2) the legacy fallback does not originate the staleness: the default fingerprint already diverges before validity dispatch, and both legacy recomputations also preserve the reason raw and fail to match. (3) a broken normalizer is excluded: the same normalizer maps `docs only ` and `docs only\\n` to `docs only`; it simply is never applied at lines 129-134.\n\nSecurity negative controls remain material: interior double space (`docs  only`) => `51c2845a17a03ffc`; word change (`runtime only`) => `d0fa333084ea6672`; both produce `stale-material`. `normalize_insignificant_whitespace()` leaves both unchanged, so reusing it does not collapse meaningful reason edits. Existing 2be7/94a3/96d1 suites all pass today (58 tests), confirming this is an uncovered parity gap rather than a broken description fix.\n\nLegitimacy: defect/incomplete parity implementation. Parent `unspirited-polished-arcticfox` deliberately filed this sibling in its completed parity sweep. Its authoritative invariant is implemented and documented at `material_diff.py:65-82`, `pass1.py:742-755`, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md:455-479`: whitespace carrying no plan substance is normalized out, while meaningful material edits invalidate. The other free-text material field violates that invariant.\n\nCaller-dependency sweep: Serena + rg show `material_basis` feeds only `material_components` and `material_fingerprint`; the latter feeds review generation/snapshots and validity recomputation. Those consumers depend only on consistent current hashes and benefit from the correction. One real behavioral dependency must be preserved: `_legacy_material_ok` (`attest.py:645-670`) deliberately reproduces pre-330c raw and post-330c/pre-2be7 checkbox-only generations. Both must continue hashing the reason raw.\n\nAdditional compatibility finding: the fix creates a new historical boundary. A post-2be7/pre-reason-fix attestation was signed with canonical DESCRIPTION but raw REASON. For a signed trailing-space reason, the old-current hash is `bc423348886c26f3`, while both existing legacy candidates are `12e291cb05bacc64` because they also change description canonicalization. Neither can grandfather that unchanged attestation after reason normalization. Phase 2 must preserve this third generation explicitly (canonical description + raw reason), in addition to keeping pre-330c raw behavior.\n\nPhase 1 stops here; no source/test edit, claim, plan review, or transition was performed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786297988392831001,"uuid":"2d6111a1-adeb-4a8a-9b4b-9765c19dd641"}